help() {
    cat <<'USAGE'

    safesetid install_script        # install script and services
    safesetid init                  # initialize the backups
    safesetid verify                # verify allowlists and restore canonical copies if needed
    safesetid configure_uid         # edit /etc/safesetid/uid.config (opens editor, applies changes)
    safesetid configure_gid         # edit /etc/safesetid/gid.config (opens editor, applies changes)
    safesetid uninstall_script      # uninstall script and services (requires uninstall token)

Note: tmpfs is mounted at ${TEMP_STORE_DIR} when possible and used as the runtime trusted copy.
A systemd mount unit and a protector path/service ensure the wrapper will be restored
from a trusted backup if removed or changed. The script sets immutable flags (chattr +i)
when available to harden backups; uninstall removes them.

USAGE
}

case "${1:-}" in
